    "answer": "d",
    "conf": "high",
    "why": "In this proverb \"but\" means \"except\" and governs the noun phrase \"the brave\", so it is a preposition - Wren & Martin cite this very sentence as the standard example. \"But\" can also be an adverb meaning \"only\" (\"He is but a child\") or a relative pronoun (\"There is no one but knows it\"), but neither reading fits here, and \"conjunction\" is not even offered.",
