    "marked": "d",
    "answer": "d",
    "conf": "high",
    "why": "\"Like\" here takes the noun phrase \"his father\" as its object and expresses resemblance, which makes it a preposition. It would be a conjunction only if a clause with its own verb followed (\"He talks like his father does\"), and prescriptive grammar prefers \"as\" in that case - but \"conjunction\" is not an option and no clause follows.",
