    "why": "The fixed collocation is \"arrive at\" a decision, conclusion or agreement. \"Arrive in\" is used only of large places (arrive in Aizawl), and \"arrive on\" and \"arrive by\" take dates and modes of transport respectively.",
    "topic": "prepositions",
