    "why": "\"Absorbed in\" is the fixed collocation for being deeply engaged in an activity. \"Absorbed by\" exists but means taken up or swallowed by something, and \"with\" is not offered in that sense here.",
    "topic": "prepositions",
    "flag": null,
    "topicGroup": "english",
